//I used to have android:networkSecurityConfig=&quot;@xml/network_security_config&quot; here as well
</code></pre>
<p>With those changes, the app connects to the server now. But immediately after connecting, the app seems to get disconnected. Then it connects to the server again, then gets disconnected again, then connects to the server, and this cycle doesn't seem to stop. I'm getting a <code>closed client namespace disconnect</code> on the disconnects.</p>

Answers:
Here's a corrected version of the Kotlin code that uses the Socket.IO library:

```kotlin
import io.socket.client.IO
import io.socket.client.Socket

private val socket = IO.socket("http://10.0.2.2:8000/socket.io/") {
    android {
        usesCleartextTraffic = true
    }
}

fun main() {
    val socket = Socket()
    socket.connect()
    socket.on("connect", onConnect)
    socket.on("reply", onReply)

    private val onConnect = Emitter.Listener {
        Log.i("Socket", "onConnect")
        socket.emit("notice", "{\"relay_num\": 4, \"to_status\": 1}")
    }

    private val onReply = Emitter.Listener {
        Log.i("Socket", "onReply")
        Log.d("Socket", "reply: ${it[0]}")
    }
}
```

And here's the corrected version of the Android code that uses the Socket.IO library:

```kotlin
import io.socket.client.IO
import io.socket.client.Socket

init {
    try {
        val socket = IO.socket("http://10.0.2.2:8000/socket.io/") {
            android {
                usesCleartextTraffic = true
            }
        }
    } catch (e: ConnectException) {
        Log.e("Socket", "Socket ConnectExc: ${e.localizedMessage}")
    } catch (e: URISyntaxException) {
        Log.e("Socket", "Socket URISynExc: ${e.localizedMessage}")
    } catch (e: Exception) {
        Log.e("Socket", "Socket Exc: ${e.localizedMessage}")
    }
}

fun main() {
    val socket = Socket()
    socket.connect()
    socket.on("connect", onConnect)
    socket.on("reply", onReply)

    private val onConnect = Emitter.Listener {
        Log.i("Socket", "onConnect")
        socket.emit("notice", "{\"relay_num\": 4, \"to_status\": 1}")
    }

    private val onReply = Emitter.Listener {
        Log.i("Socket", "onReply")
        Log.d("Socket", "reply: ${it[0]}")
    }
}
```

