Title: How can I fix the &#39;TransportBindingElement&#39; error when consuming a web service in .NET Core with default binding?.
Body: <p>I am tring to consume a web service in my dotnet core7 project.
I don't have access to the service itself.
When I am trying to call a service method it returns that error:</p>
<p>The CustomBinding on the ServiceEndpoint with contract 'IMyService' lacks a TransportBindingElement.<br />
Every binding must have at least one binding element that derives from TransportBindingElement.'</p>
<p>While it uses default binding in reference.</p>
<p>How can I fix it.</p>
<p>I tried overrite the client configuration. but it also didn't work.
private static System.ServiceModel.Channels.Binding GetBindingForEndpoint(TimeSpan timeout)
{
var httpsBinding = new BasicHttpsBinding();
httpsBinding.Security.Transport.ClientCredentialType = HttpClientCredentialType.Basic;
httpsBinding.Security.Mode = BasicHttpsSecurityMode.Transport;</p>
<pre><code>        var integerMaxValue = int.MaxValue;
        httpsBinding.MaxBufferSize = integerMaxValue;
        httpsBinding.MaxReceivedMessageSize = integerMaxValue;
        httpsBinding.ReaderQuotas = System.Xml.XmlDictionaryReaderQuotas.Max;
        httpsBinding.AllowCookies = true;

        httpsBinding.ReceiveTimeout = timeout;
        httpsBinding.SendTimeout = timeout;
        httpsBinding.OpenTimeout = timeout;
        httpsBinding.CloseTimeout = timeout;

        return httpsBinding;
    }
</code></pre>
<p>And in creating client:
_RedemptionServiceClient = new RedemptionLiteIntegrationServiceClient(&quot;https://78.93.37.230:9799/RedemptionLiteIntegrationServiceBasicHttpEndPoint&quot;, new TimeSpan(1, 30, 0),&quot;&quot;,&quot;&quot;);</p>

Answers:
```python
import socket
from socket import SSL
from typing import Dict
from datetime import timedelta

class CustomBinding:
    def __init__(self, transport: str, security: str, mode: str):
        self.transport = transport
        self.security = security
        self.mode = mode

class TransportBindingElement:
    def __init__(self, mode: str):
        self.mode = mode

class BasicHttpsBinding:
    def __init__(self):
        self.transport = None
        self.security = None
        self.mode = None

    def set_transport(self, transport: str):
        self.transport = transport

    def set_security(self, security: str):
        self.security = security

    def set_mode(self, mode: str):
        self.mode = mode

    def get_max_buffer_size(self) -> int:
        return 1024 * 1024

    def get_max_received_message_size(self) -> int:
        return 1024 * 1024

    def get_reader_quotas(self) -> Dict[str, int]:
        return {"MaxMessageSize": self.get_max_received_message_size()}

    def get_allow_cookies(self) -> bool:
        return True

    def get_receive_timeout(self) -> timedelta:
        return timedelta(seconds=1)

    def get_send_timeout(self) -> timedelta:
        return timedelta(seconds=1)

    def get_open_timeout(self) -> timedelta:
        return timedelta(seconds=1)

    def get_close_timeout(self) -> timedelta:
        return timedelta(seconds=1)


def get_client_config(timeout: timedelta) -> Dict[str, str]:
    return {
        'TransportBindingElement': TransportBindingElement('Transport'),
        'Security': 'BasicHttp',
        'Mode': 'Transport',
        'SecurityMode': 'Transport',
        'SecurityProtocol': 'TLS',
        'SecurityCredentials': 'Basic',
        'MaxBufferSize': str(get_client_max_buffer_size()),
        'MaxReceivedMessageSize': str(get_client_max_received_message_size()),
        'ReaderQuotas': str(get_client_reader_quotas()),
        'AllowCookies': 'True',
        'ReceiveTimeout': str(get_client_receive_timeout()),
        'SendTimeout': str(get_client_send_timeout()),
        'OpenTimeout': str(get_client_open_timeout()),
        'CloseTimeout': str(get_client_close_timeout())
    }


def get_client_max_buffer_size():
    return 1024 * 1024


def get_client_max_received_message_size():
    return 1024 * 1024


def get_client_reader_quotas():
    return {'MaxMessageSize': get_client_max_received_message_size()}


def get_client_allow_cookies():
    return True


def get_client_receive_timeout():
    return timedelta(seconds=1)


def get_client_send_timeout():
    return timedelta(seconds=1)


def get_client_open_timeout():
    return timedelta(seconds=1)


def get_client_close_timeout():
    return timedelta(seconds=1)


def create_client_config(timeout: timedelta) -> Dict[str, str]:
    return get_client_config(timeout)


def create_client(max_buffer_size: int, max_received_message_size: int, reader_quotas: Dict[str, int], allow_cookies: bool, receive_timeout: timedelta, send_timeout: timedelta, open_timeout: timedelta, close_timeout: timedelta):
    return {
        'TransportBindingElement': TransportBindingElement('Transport'),
        'Security': 'BasicHttp',
        'Mode': 'Transport',
        'SecurityMode': 'Transport',
        'SecurityProtocol': 'TLS',
        'SecurityCredentials': 'Basic',
        'MaxBufferSize': str(max_buffer_size),
        'MaxReceivedMessageSize': str(max_received_message_size),
        'ReaderQuotas': str(reader_quotas),
        'AllowCookies': str(allow_cookies),
        'ReceiveTimeout': str(receive_timeout),
        'SendTimeout': str(send_timeout),
        'OpenTimeout': str(open_timeout),
        'CloseTimeout': str(close_timeout)
    }


def create_client_with_default_config(timeout: timedelta):
    return create_client_config(timeout)


# Usage
client_config = create_client_with_default_config(datetime.timedelta(seconds=30))
client_max_buffer_size = get_client_max_buffer_size()
client_max_received_message_size = get_client_max_received_message_size()
reader_quotas = get_client_reader_quotas()
allow_cookies = get_client_allow_cookies()
receive_timeout = timedelta(seconds=1)
send_timeout = timedelta(seconds=1)
open_timeout = timedelta(seconds=1)
close_timeout = timedelta(seconds=1)

basicHttpsBinding = BasicHttpsBinding()
basicHttpsBinding.set_transport('https')
basicHttpsBinding.set_security('BasicHttp')
basicHttpsBinding.set_mode('Transport')

client_config = create_client_config(datetime.timedelta(seconds=30))
basicHttpsBinding.set_max_buffer_size(client_max_buffer_size)
basicHttpsBinding.set_max_received_message_size(client_max_received_message_size)
basicHttpsBinding.set_reader_quotas(reader_quotas)
basicHttpsBinding.set_allow_cookies(allow_cookies)
basicHttpsBinding.set_receive_timeout(receive_timeout)
basicHttpsBinding.set_send_timeout(send_timeout)
basicHttpsBinding.set_open_timeout(open_timeout)
basicHttpsBinding.set_close_timeout(close_timeout)

redemptionServiceClient = RedemptionLiteIntegrationServiceClient('https://78.93.37.230:9799/RedemptionLiteIntegrationServiceBasicHttpEndPoint', client_config, allow_cookies, receive_timeout, send_timeout, open_timeout, close_timeout)
```

The issue is that the `TransportBindingElement` class does not have a `TransportBindingElement` attribute, but you are trying to set it in the `BasicHttpsBinding` class. This is why you are getting the `TransportBindingElement` attribute error.

To fix this, you should create a separate class for the `TransportBindingElement` class. Here's how you can do it:

```python
class TransportBindingElement:
    def __init__(self, mode: str):
        self.mode = mode
```

And then use it in the `BasicHttpsBinding` class like this:

```python
basicHttpsBinding.set_transport(TransportBindingElement('Transport'))
```

With this change, the code should work as expected.

