Title: How can i use React toastify (Promise) toast, with email js.
Body: <p>I am currently using success and error toast with email js
but i want to use toastify promise with my custom loader here is my current code</p>
<pre><code>import emailjs from &quot;@emailjs/browser&quot;;
import { toast } from 'react-toastify';

export const sendEmail = ({ service_id, templete_id, values, theme, setIsloading, pubkey }) =&gt; {
  emailjs.send(service_id, templete_id, values, pubkey).then(
    () =&gt; {
        toast.success(&quot;Application submitted !&quot;, {theme})
        setIsloading(false);
    },
    (error) =&gt; {
      console.error(error);
      toast.error(&quot;Something went wrong.&quot;, {theme});
      setIsloading(false);

    }
  );
};
</code></pre>
<pre><code>const resolveWithSomeData = new Promise(resolve =&gt; setTimeout(() =&gt; resolve(&quot;world&quot;), 3000));
toast.promise(
    resolveWithSomeData,
    {
      pending: {
        render(){
          return &quot;I'm loading&quot;
        },
        icon: false,
      },
      success: {
        render({data}){
          return `Hello ${data}`
        },
        // other options
        icon: &quot;🟢&quot;,
      },
      error: {
        render({data}){
          // When the promise reject, data will contains the error
          return &lt;MyErrorComponent message={data.message} /&gt;
        }
      }
    }
)
</code></pre>
<p>i found this but it couldnt resolving my issue I want a custom loader on pending status</p>

Answers:
Here's an updated version of your code with a custom loader for the pending status:

```javascript
import emailjs from "@emailjs/browser";
import { toast } from "react-toastify";

export const sendEmail = ({ service_id, template_id, values, theme, setIsloading, pubkey }) => {
  emailjs.send(service_id, template_id, values, pubkey).then(() => {
    toast.success("Application submitted!", { theme });
    setIsloading(false);
  }, (error) => {
    console.error(error);
    toast.error("Something went wrong.", { theme });
    setIsloading(false);
  });
};

const customLoader = () => {
  return toast.promise(
    new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(() => resolve("Loading..."), 3000)),
    {
      pending: {
        render() => <p>Loading...</p>,
        icon: false,
      },
      success: {
        render({ data }) => data,
        // other options
        icon: "🔄",
      },
      error: {
        render({ data }) => <p>Error: {data.message}</p>,
        onAction: () => {
          console.error(data);
        },
      },
    }
  );
};

const resolveWithSomeData = new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(() => resolve("world"), 3000));
const pendingResolve = customLoader();

toast.promise(
  pendingResolve,
  {
    pending: {
      render() => <p>Loading...</p>,
      icon: false,
    },
    success: {
      render({ data }) => data,
      // other options
      icon: "🔄",
    },
    error: {
      render({ data }) => <p>Error: {data.message}</p>,
      onAction: () => {
        console.error(data);
      },
    },
  }
);
```

In this updated code, I've created a custom loader function `customLoader` that returns a promise that resolves after a 3-second delay. The `pendingResolve` promise is used to display the "Loading..." message during the pending state. I've also updated the `sendEmail` function to use the `customLoader` promise.

